Pull Requests
1. Open the repository on GitHub.
2. Select "Compare & pull request" for the pushed branch.
3. Set the base branch to `main` and review the changed files.
4. Add a clear title and describe the change, tests, and any follow-up work.
5. Create the pull request and request a review.
6. Address review comments by committing and pushing additional changes to the same branch.
7. After approval and passing checks, merge the pull request into `main`.
8. Delete the feature branch after it has been merged.

Update the local main branch after merging
git checkout main
git pull origin main
